USE ../knowledge/summary-knowledge.flow
USE ../knowledge/draft-knowledge.flow
USE ../knowledge/tool-knowledge.flow

DO Resolve the explicit project or current checkout and active ticket from
    @request or conversation. Reject supplied-ID mismatches. Return an object
    with project, ticket_id (NULL if unknown), and ticket (complete matching
    cached Jira object or NULL). AS task_context

IF @task_context.ticket_id == NULL
    ASK "Which Jira ticket should this work use?" AS ticket_input
    DO Validate @ticket_input against the active task and return @task_context
        updated with that one Jira ID. AS task_context

SET project = @task_context.project
SET ticket_id = @task_context.ticket_id
SET ticket = @task_context.ticket

DO Retain the verified project, ticket ID, and any complete cached ticket as
    this conversation's active task without remote calls or task files.

DO Resolve and read the technical-summary.md draft for @project and @ticket_id under
    @draft_rules. Require an existing selected draft.
    Return an object with path and text. AS draft_state

SET draft_path = @draft_state.path
SET saved_draft = @draft_state.text

DO Verify @request explicitly requests publication and @saved_draft has the
    matching @ticket_id with complete, placeholder-free content satisfying
    @summary_rules. Do not create or rewrite invalid content.

DO Resolve private absolute acli and adf using @tool_guidance.
    Return an object with acli and adf. AS tools

RUN @tools.acli jira workitem comment list --key @ticket_id --json --paginate
AS comments_result

DO Parse @comments_result.stdout as JSON. Check for duplicate summaries and
    material clarifications. Return an object with Boolean
    evidence_contradicts_summary and identical_comment, and duplicate_url.
    Never replace unrelated comments. AS comment_state

IF @comment_state.evidence_contradicts_summary == TRUE
    RETURN "Publication stopped: Jira evidence contradicts the summary. Run /inux ts improve with the new evidence; the draft is unchanged."

IF @comment_state.identical_comment == FALSE
    DO Publish @saved_draft as one bounded transaction. Follow @tool_guidance.
        Create one unique private temporary directory and .adf output path. Run @tools.adf
        with the separate arguments @draft_path and that path; verify the
        ADF faithfully represents @saved_draft. Immediately verify the active
        project and ticket still match @project and @ticket_id, and re-read the
        draft. Do not publish if it differs from @saved_draft. Then run @tools.acli with the separate
        arguments jira, workitem, comment, create, --key, @ticket_id, --body-file,
        the ADF path, and --json. Parse and verify the comment or ticket URL,
        looking it up only when absent. Remove only the unique temporary directory
        before completing or failing. Return the verified URL. AS publication_url
ELSE
    SET publication_url = @comment_state.duplicate_url

DO Verify @publication_url identifies the published or identical existing
    comment for @ticket_id. Do not remove the Markdown on an uncertain result.

DO Apply verified-publication cleanup to @draft_path under @draft_rules,
    preserving it if it no longer matches @saved_draft. Return the cleanup result
    including any retained path. AS cleanup_result

PRINT Report @ticket_id, @publication_url or verified duplicate status, and @cleanup_result briefly.
